From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pratinav Seth <pratinav.seth@lexsi.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] neox: read the unembedding from lm_head when embed_out is gone

transformers renamed GPTNeoXForCausalLM.embed_out to lm_head (TransformerLens
reports the change at 5.13 in one place and 5.14 in another). 3.8.0 reads
embed_out only, so every GPT-NeoX / Pythia checkpoint fails in
convert_neox_weights with AttributeError on the transformers versions CircuitKIT
requires (>=5.15). Same change as the HookedTransformer half of the upstream fix
released in 3.9.0; hasattr-based, so it does not depend on the exact version.

diff --git a/transformer_lens/pretrained/weight_conversions/neox.py b/transformer_lens/pretrained/weight_conversions/neox.py
index 70d8a6b..76827ed 100644
--- a/transformer_lens/pretrained/weight_conversions/neox.py
+++ b/transformer_lens/pretrained/weight_conversions/neox.py
@@ -54,6 +54,9 @@ def convert_neox_weights(neox, cfg: HookedTransformerConfig):
     state_dict["ln_final.w"] = neox.gpt_neox.final_layer_norm.weight
     state_dict["ln_final.b"] = neox.gpt_neox.final_layer_norm.bias
 
-    state_dict["unembed.W_U"] = neox.embed_out.weight.T
+    # transformers renamed GPTNeoXForCausalLM.embed_out to lm_head (5.13/5.14);
+    # read whichever the installed transformers exposes.
+    unembed = neox.lm_head if hasattr(neox, "lm_head") else neox.embed_out
+    state_dict["unembed.W_U"] = unembed.weight.T
     state_dict["unembed.b_U"] = torch.zeros(cfg.d_vocab, dtype=cfg.dtype)
     return state_dict
